// B2 course (B1 → B2 roadmap), module 6 „Tööelu” (b1b2-026…030), stage B2-.
// Lesson template v4 (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12). One storyline, a year after the B1 course: Sofia leads the
// new Tartu warehouse project of Tuul Logistika — until March as acting project manager, because her B2 exam is still
// ahead (B2 module 1: Liis offered her the lead if she reaches B2 by March). One goal said on the first sheet: at the end
// the learner gives a one-minute presentation at the management meeting (Harno B2 speaking: a 1-min monologue on a work
// topic) and writes a semi-formal letter of about 140 words to the partner company Emajõe Ehitus (029 Kasuta).
// Grammar (B2, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md §5): the essive -na for a role, a time of life and „as what” — töötan
// juhina, olin seal tõlgina, esinen eraisikuna, kasutan seda näitena, lapsena elasin… — against the translative of change
// (sai juhiks, määratakse projektijuhiks, peab tähtsaks): taught in 026 (notice, table, sort, listening, forms, cloze), met
// again in 027 (job ads, error fix), 028 (Kolleegina…, Projektijuhina…, asendajana) and 029 (katseprojektina, esimese
// sammuna, the final presentation and letter). Module 5's words return: seisukoht, ilmselt, vaevalt, kindlasti, kahtlema,
// ettepanek, otsus, argument, esiteks, seetõttu, seega, kuigi, siiski, samas, nõustuma, eelistama, kompromiss,
// täpsustama, katseprojekt, tööaeg, võrdlema, eelis, puudus, seevastu, kriteerium, kaaluma.
//   026 The intranet news on the project team (roles in the essive); Gert shows the Tartu building site (listening), the
//       project manager's job description (4-option cloze), a 1-min monologue; the first team meeting in Tartu — the
//       team's cards, trainee Laura's questions, Sofia's opening words and a mail to the team.
//   027 The Tartu career fair: three visitors and their criteria (listening); what employees value (cloze), three job
//       ads and ten job seekers, a job interview with Gert; Laura has three offers — advice from Sofia, a 1-min
//       monologue and Laura's semi-formal letter to the employer she chooses.
//   028 Overtime: Gert and Markus quarrel in the project chat; a Harno B2 article on conflicts at work (MC), the team
//       coach's advice (forms in a text); two voice messages, Sofia's talk with Markus, her meeting with Liis and the
//       written agreement.
//   029 Sofia's performance review with Liis — workload and a hybrid-work idea (listening); a sentence-bank article and
//       radio voices on hybrid work, a debate with pro / contra cards; the final project: the management meeting
//       (one-minute presentation, a decision) and the reply to Andres Kivi of Emajõe Ehitus.
// Lesson 5 (030) is the module's check in Harno B2 form (unchanged). The v3 file is in archive/v3/b2/module06.js.
